# PBRM metallic/roughness shader.
#
# No conditions: whether a shape uses this depends on whether a .pbrm RESOLVED
# for its material and whether the PBR workflow is on, and neither is expressible
# as a .prog check (those evaluate NIF data only). Renderer::setupProgram selects
# it explicitly by name, so leaving the condition list empty keeps it out of the
# automatic scan — an empty list never matches there.
#
# The vertex stage is fo4_default.vert as-is: it already supplies every varying
# this pass needs (LightDir, ViewDir, texCoord, A/C/D, btnMatrix, reflMatrix), so
# there is nothing for a private copy to do except drift out of step with it.

shaders fo4_default.vert pbrm_default.frag
